  "commit": "f064592642d7fcef3260ea62eb22981b0ef8d471",
  "description": "THE ITERATION AN ADVERSARIAL CONSULTATION PAID FOR. run/0021 closed on its own ledger pass; this run is everything that followed from asking a Fable agent to attack the belief that the remaining v1 work is entirely owner-gated. Four of its findings were verified against the tree first-hand before anything was touched, and three of the four were worse than the report said.\n\nWHAT THE MERGES ARE. #374 rewrote the operations runbook's Trash section, which told an operator the opposite of the code on the one irreversible operation in the product: trash purge refuses BECAUSE a period is archived, where period purge REQUIRES it, there is no retention window at that door at all, and the directory purge the page described does not exist. #376 gave Run.merges a field pair per main-push workflow and a guard that refuses if the set drifts. #378 deleted a directory literally named `undefined` that had been shipping 16,681 unreferenced bytes into every image layer, and made the class refuse. #379 corrected four texts the tree contradicts, two of them worse than reported.\n\nTHE RUN BOUNDARY IS ITSELF A FINDING, recorded in run/0021's closing note: nothing triggers it, so it drifts open until somebody decides. This run is opened deliberately rather than inherited, and startTime is the loop trigger's own firing time (2026-09-21T20:44:58Z) rather than a round number -- 23 seconds after run/0021's close, which is also what makes it strictly after, as the validator requires.\n\nMY OWN TWO MISTAKES THIS RUN, both caught by CI on #376 and both worth the space. I inserted a constant BETWEEN checkMergeEntry()'s docblock and its signature, orphaning the `@param list<string>` and costing phpstan the by-ref type at the call site. And I rewrote two blocks that .github/mutations.json registers by exact source text, which mutation-check caught and named precisely. The second was repointed, not weakened: same expectFailing tests, and each new `remove` text was applied to a copy of the validator and shown to silence it -- because \"I updated the registry to match\" is the sentence a weakened guard would also produce.",
